{"base_rate":0.14869888475836432,"brier":0.08643698884758365,"bss":0.317176097161572,"bss_hi":0.4889660689816063,"bss_lo":0.12714030014488145,"chart":{"base":[190.5,158.6],"fp":[231.3,123.3],"lead":"62,252.3 272,245.5 482,237.7 692,223.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.32 — higher than 59% of cities","fp":"low end +1pp, high end +28pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 51% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 4%; promised 76% → rained 58%"},"rel":"79.6,448.9 543.1,216.3"},"country":"NE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.046933085501858755,"ess":221.4465574285923,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Maradi</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Maradi rain forecast is moderately skilful, and honest except at one point on the scale.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (96%), believe about\n<b>64%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 538 days, 2024-05-11 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 4.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.32, ranked 88 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(24&ndash;170) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>374</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'><b>52%</b></td><td class='num'>54</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 of 4 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Maradi</b> <span class=\"muted\">Niger</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;15% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 15% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">honest except at one point</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.32</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>24&ndash;170\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>538 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Maradi &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Maradi\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.116898395721925,378.10695187165777 127.51272727272726,269.4909090909091 258.4033333333333,132.59259259259258 396.93890909090914,18.0 396.93890909090914,51.09090909090912 258.4033333333333,226.96296296296296 127.51272727272726,348.9090909090909 59.116898395721925,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"327.8736059479554\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"327.8736059479554\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.116898395721925,378.10695187165777 127.51272727272726,295.9636363636364 258.4033333333333,193.25925925925927 396.93890909090914,150.36363636363637\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 374 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"59.116898395721925\" cy=\"378.10695187165777\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 55 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"127.51272727272726\" cy=\"295.9636363636364\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 57%&amp;#10;It rained 52% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 54 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"258.4033333333333\" cy=\"193.25925925925927\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 55 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"396.93890909090914\" cy=\"150.36363636363637\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(15%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Not enough days in this city's record to split the year into four and still say anything defensible about each part. The split is shown only where it is supported.</p>\n"},"lat":13.5,"lon":7.10174,"n":538,"n_cities":216,"name":"Maradi","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.09,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003155080213903744,"n":374,"obs":0.0106951871657754,"sig":false},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.09,"mean":0.19636363636363632,"n":55,"obs":0.23636363636363636,"sig":false},{"hi":0.82,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.5661111111111111,"n":54,"obs":0.5185185185185185,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.82,"mean":0.9574545454545456,"n":55,"obs":0.6363636363636364,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.1,"provisional":false,"rank":88,"rank_hi":170.0,"rank_lo":24.0,"reliability":0.01097033739612026,"resolution":0.052064763999938694,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"maradi","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Niamey"}